<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pino III Ordelaffi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1436–<a href="/years/1480">1480</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pino III Ordelaffi was lord of Forlì in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a> from 1466 until his death in 1480, one of the last rulers of the Ordelaffi family that had governed the city since the 13th century. He strengthened the fortress of Ravaldino. On his death <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-sixtus-iv">Pope Sixtus IV</a> granted Forlì to his own nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girolamo-riario">Girolamo Riario</a>, ending Ordelaffi rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pino-iii-ordelaffi.jpg" alt="Pino III Ordelaffi" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sailko · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Musei_di_San_Domenico,_francesco_di_simone_ferrucci,_pino_III_oderlaffi_1470-80_02.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
